  "fig_no": 11,
  "caption": "Proof dependency graph. Each grey solid edge $A\\to B$ means ``$B$'s proof uses $A$''. The two red dashed edges form a bootstrapping cycle between the kernel-stability bounds (Lemma~\\ref{lem:helpful_bounds} Parts~5,~9--13), the FFN drift (Lemma~\\ref{lem:ffn_drift}), and the convergence theorem (Theorem~\\ref{thm:convergence}); we close this cycle via the stop-time argument of Remark~\\ref{rem:stop_time}. The lower bounds (Theorems~\\ref{thm:lower_stat}, \\ref{thm:lower_opt}) feed into the two-sided scaling-law bound (Theorem~\\ref{thm:scaling_law}) but do not enter the bootstrap."
 }
